{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.48392793328969386, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["Nothing here tries to get around the measurement. The new code reads no files, pastes no answers and never uses test labels. The LightGBM models are fit only on the training features F and the standardized training target yz, and only predict on the test features Ft.", "No bug makes the result meaningless. The SVR and LightGBM predictions are both on the same standardized scale, so averaging them is consistent. Spearman ignores rescaling anyway. Each LightGBM model's random_state comes from the seed argument.", "The diff doesn't show `import lightgbm as lgb`. Since the job finished with a score, the import must already be in the file outside the diff context. Worth confirming in the file.", "My z is about -0.091, using the stated noise sd of 0.0070 for one run on each side: (0.4830 - 0.4839) / (0.0070 * sqrt(2)). The reported -0.094 is a little larger in size, probably from unrounded run values. The sign and the conclusion are the same.", "The candidate is 0.0009 worse than the incumbent, well inside the noise. It also adds about 5x400 boosting rounds of runtime and extra code. The provisional reject is consistent with the numbers and with 'simpler is better'."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Blend the existing kernel SVR 50/50 with an average of 5 seed-bagged LightGBM regressors (subsample 0.7, colsample 0.3, lr 0.03, 15 leaves, 400 trees) trained on Morgan bits plus standardized descriptors.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "spruce", "idea_id": "b047", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_clear_HH_1_cs0-candidate-23_1795049523350", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0320324, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0320324, "latency_s": 6.756926217, "requested_model": "sonn